The files in this directory are output from Gaussian 16, used only as test input
for the parser. They are not covered by this project's LGPL-3.0-or-later licence,
and the program text they contain, including the citation block at the top of each
file, belongs to Gaussian, Inc.

They hold results for small textbook molecules (water, formaldehyde, methanol,
ethane, benzene, dioxygen) and no research data. tools/sanitize_gaussian_log.py
removed the licence banner, paths, user and machine names, dates and timings.

To regenerate them you need your own licensed copy of Gaussian.
